{
  "paraphrase": "Princess Märtha Louise of Norway, daughter of one of Europe’s longest-reigning monarchs, married California-based self-described sixth-generation shaman Durek Verrett in Geiranger on Saturday. Although the ceremony differed from a typical royal wedding, crowds still gathered in the cloudy streets hoping to see the couple. Märtha Louise, 52, the only daughter of King Harald and Queen Sonja and fourth in line to the throne, wed Verrett, 49, in a traditional Church of Norway service at the Hotel Union near the Geiranger fjord. She was accompanied by seven bridesmaids, including her teenage daughters, Leah and Emma Behn, from her previous marriage to the late writer Ari Behn, which ended in divorce in 2017. Around 350 guests attended, among them senior Norwegian royals as well as Crown Princess Victoria and Prince Daniel of Sweden, and Prince Constantijn and Princess Laurentien of the Netherlands. Märtha Louise has long followed an unconventional path for a royal, previously describing herself as clairvoyant and operating a healing school focused on communicating with angels. In 2022, she said she would give up official royal duties to concentrate on shared business ventures with Verrett and to draw a clearer line between those activities and Norway’s royal family. Verrett, who calls himself a servant of God and an energy activator on Instagram, counts Gwyneth Paltrow among his high-profile clients."
}
```

